# Percentage comparison within one qualification

Verifies equality and ordering between two percentage values without any scaling. Comparing 10% against 25% exercises `==`, `!=`, `<`, and `>`, while the reflexive `<=` and `>=` cases pin the boundary where both operands are equal.

>>> source
low: decimal = 10%
high: decimal = 25%
print(low == high)
print(low != high)
print(low < high)
print(high > low)
print(low <= low)
print(high >= high)

<<< stdout
false
true
true
true
true
true

<<< stderr
